1
00:02:04,130 --> 00:02:08,640
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:09,425 --> 00:02:27,355
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:36,000
Your escrows are secured, father.

4
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:42,320
These souvenirs which once belonged
to our ancestors...

5
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:45,160
... will be studied...

6
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:48,380
... infused...

7
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:55,520
... and eventually will turn into new
conquests and cities.

8
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:02,600
I know that I have more responsibilities
now.

9
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:07,480
I also know that I need to be more
diligent.

10
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:11,220
The night and the morning shall become
one.

11
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:16,960
From now on, inattention is illicit for
all of us.

12
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:50,080
My children.

13
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,940
My children!

14
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:17,280
Do we have your permission, Bamsı Bey?

15
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:22,460
You may come in.

16
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,440
Bamsı Bey?

17
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:02,400
Isn't he here?

18
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:08,080
He will be here soon.

19
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:15,240
Then we shall take a seat and wait
for him.

20
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:17,840
Stop.

21
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:28,520
Does Bamsı Bey even like you?

22
00:06:31,780 --> 00:06:34,680
I wouldn't like to be rebuked by him.

23
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:36,300
Yes, he does.

24
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:41,240
I mean I suppose he likes us.

25
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:48,100
Bamsı Bey is indeed a hospitable person.

26
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:55,660
We shall wait and see.

27
00:07:13,960 --> 00:07:14,940
Cerkutay!

28
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:21,140
What are you doing with those
swords, Cerkutay?

29
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:22,560
Put them away at once!

30
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:37,060
Greetings to you.

31
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,400
Thank you.

32
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:42,480
Greetings to you too.

33
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:07,660
You are indeed welcomed at this
time of night.

34
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:18,160
You may tell me the reason you are here.

35
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,280
Bamsı Bey.

36
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:27,980
Oh, mighty Bamsı Bey.

37
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:34,280
You don't know me.

38
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:42,919
However, I have never forgotten you.

39
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:49,240
And I just can't forget.

40
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:56,380
With deceased Ertuğrul Bey...

41
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:01,700
... you saved the life of my father.

42
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:12,780
I was a little child back then.

43
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,260
In order to save my life...

44
00:09:24,420 --> 00:09:26,240
... you stood against a sword.

45
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:34,400
The mark of that sword strike...

46
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:37,940
... can still be seen on your neck.

47
00:10:00,380 --> 00:10:02,020
I remember now.

48
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:09,160
I can indeed recall you.

49
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:14,400
Thank you. May you live long.

50
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:18,900
Please have a seat.

51
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:32,180
With your excuse, Bamsı Bey.

52
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:35,960
It's not a problem.

53
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:45,220
I remember you.

54
00:10:45,540 --> 00:10:52,080
May his soul rest in peace, my Ertuğrul
Bey named you after Süleyman Shah.

55
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:54,640
Süleyman.

56
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:59,600
Thanks to Allah...

57
00:11:01,520 --> 00:11:04,420
... we are now partners with the Kayı.

58
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:10,080
Dündar Bey is helping us.

59
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:21,200
From now on, when our Osman Bey leaves
for numerous battles and conquests...

60
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:25,460
... he won't have to think about trade.

61
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:30,200
How magnificent. I wish you good luck
and blessed profits.

62
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:40,700
However, may you never give place to
illicit profit in your business.

63
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:45,840
May you keep this Tent away from
illicit doings.

64
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,380
Alright?

65
00:11:52,700 --> 00:11:54,080
Do you get it?

66
00:11:54,980 --> 00:11:57,820
Don't worry, Bamsı Bey.

67
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:03,720
Cerkutay.

68
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:08,280
We shall offer something to our guests.

69
00:12:09,360 --> 00:12:10,760
Tell me.

70
00:12:10,780 --> 00:12:13,540
Would you like to drink ayran or sherbet?

71
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:18,640
To tell you the truth...

72
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:23,860
... it's impossible for them to
drink sherbet, my Bey.

73
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:27,580
Why is that, Cerkutay?

74
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:30,860
Why can't they drink sherbet?

75
00:12:36,620 --> 00:12:38,340
I drank all the sherbet.

76
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:50,160
So you drank a full jug of sherbet,
Cerkutay?

77
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:55,060
I was a bit hot and thirsty, my Bey.

78
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:57,960
So I drank it all.

79
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:00,700
-You were hot?
-Yes, my Bey.

80
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:09,740
It's not important, Bamsı Bey.

81
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:14,600
While we are here, we thought it'd be
good to visit you.

82
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:16,860
If you say so.

83
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:21,940
May Allah make your way clear.

84
00:13:22,580 --> 00:13:24,160
-Amin.
-Thank you.

85
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:27,780
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

86
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:35,140
Don't bother.

87
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:42,060
Thank you.

88
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:46,400
So that you won't drink anything, may
Allah make your way clear.

89
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:25,100
We ate a lot at the meeting.

90
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:27,100
Yes, brother, indeed we did.

91
00:14:33,420 --> 00:14:34,880
Boran.

92
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:38,060
Are you thinking about your brother?

93
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:43,280
Tell me if you're thinking about
Head-Alp Göktuğ.

94
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:45,440
Yes, I am.

95
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:48,240
I wish he was here with us.

96
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:54,280
He doesn't even know that I'm about
to get engaged.

97
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:02,940
Oh, my Bey!

98
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:05,980
Welcome, my veteran Bey.

99
00:15:06,220 --> 00:15:07,440
Thank you.

100
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:10,160
Who did you fight against, my Bey?

101
00:15:11,060 --> 00:15:12,660
Don't ask, Gence Bey.

102
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:16,920
No matter how hard you train, fighting
for real is very different.

103
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,280
He who stands against you also
swings a sword, right?

104
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:28,600
They wanted to kill me.

105
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:36,980
From now on, I will be present at any
clash that will take place.

106
00:15:38,840 --> 00:15:41,240
Don't you ever dare to leave without me.

107
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:02,260
Is sleeping has become illicit for
you, my Osman?

108
00:17:06,160 --> 00:17:09,339
People have given us the honor to
serve, my Bala.

109
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:16,819
Besides, when we die, we will have lots
of time to sleep.

110
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:59,080
Dinner is ready, my Bey.

111
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,980
Thank you, my Bala.

112
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:24,100
May your hands do not see any trouble.

113
00:18:36,180 --> 00:18:37,720
Allow me, my Bey.

114
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:43,660
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

115
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:29,300
My Bala.

116
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:33,060
You already have many things to do.

117
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:35,680
And soon you will become even busier.

118
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:38,940
You can get more helpers if you want.

119
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:41,120
No.

120
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:45,380
I need no helper when it comes to
serving you.

121
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:49,740
Serving you is not a burden but
honor for me.

122
00:19:56,800 --> 00:20:02,540
With you permission, I'd like to open a
workshop for the poor in Söğüt.

123
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:08,420
What a wonderful thought.

124
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:12,200
What a wonderful plan.

125
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:15,900
By doing so, I'd also like to raise
skillful women.

126
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:18,700
Perhaps, with your permission.

127
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:22,660
May you take Hazal Hatun with you.

128
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:25,020
Why, my Bey?

129
00:20:25,180 --> 00:20:29,540
After all, they wanted the Beyhood
so deeply.

130
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:33,560
They tried to play games on us.

131
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:36,600
We shall give them new tasks.

132
00:20:37,780 --> 00:20:44,840
We shall give them new tasks in order
to prevent them being tricked by Devil.

133
00:20:46,560 --> 00:20:50,320
We must answer to their mischiefs with
good intentions...

134
00:20:50,380 --> 00:20:52,680
... in order not to end up like them.

135
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:56,160
As you wish, my Bey.

136
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:02,040
However, I'd like you to know that...

137
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:06,580
... if she goes beyond the limit, I will
punish her.

138
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:14,880
As long as you are fair-minded...

139
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:19,980
... you shouldn't worry about it.

140
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:26,940
Thank you, my Bey.

141
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:37,320
My Bey, also...

142
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:43,440
Also?

143
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:47,480
For our past's sake...

144
00:21:49,380 --> 00:21:52,500
... I'd like to choose the Hatun for you.

145
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:06,280
My Bala.

146
00:22:07,300 --> 00:22:08,820
My beloved Bala.

147
00:22:09,660 --> 00:22:10,780
My rose.

148
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:19,080
Every believer has a unique challenge.

149
00:22:20,780 --> 00:22:23,360
And this is the challenge of our love.

150
00:22:31,260 --> 00:22:35,820
Whatever Allah leads to us, we shall
accept it the way it is.

151
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:45,120
The duty is yours, my Bala.

152
00:25:47,860 --> 00:25:51,140
May God bless you all, loyal servants
of Jesus.

153
00:25:52,020 --> 00:25:53,340
May God bless you.

154
00:25:53,500 --> 00:25:54,480
Amen.

155
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:08,740
The feudal landlord of all Turkish
borders, fearless lord Ayos Nikola...

156
00:26:10,540 --> 00:26:12,260
... is waiting for you.

157
00:26:24,960 --> 00:26:26,600
Do I have your permission?

158
00:26:27,320 --> 00:26:29,040
You may come in, Arslan Bey.

159
00:26:37,120 --> 00:26:39,540
May your victory be blessed, Osman Bey.

160
00:26:40,140 --> 00:26:42,960
You got our revenge from them.

161
00:26:43,820 --> 00:26:49,040
You banished those heathens who tried
to take the Serhat region from us.

162
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:50,600
May you live long!

163
00:26:51,320 --> 00:26:53,340
May you live long too, Arslan Bey.

164
00:26:53,620 --> 00:26:58,620
With the grace of Allah along with
the strength and effort of our Valiants...

165
00:26:58,640 --> 00:27:00,620
... we got rid of those heathens.

166
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:03,420
Take a seat.

167
00:27:09,620 --> 00:27:11,220
How are you been doing?

168
00:27:11,260 --> 00:27:13,380
How are the conquest preparations?

169
00:27:13,420 --> 00:27:16,740
The Beys and Alps are gathering.

170
00:27:17,380 --> 00:27:19,800
And the swords are getting sharpened.

171
00:27:20,160 --> 00:27:23,640
Then, we shall help you too.

172
00:27:25,680 --> 00:27:29,140
We can't wait like this while Geyhatu
is on his way.

173
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:35,260
I say we break down the wings of heathens
located near our borders.

174
00:27:35,300 --> 00:27:38,500
Well said, Osman Bey. Well said.

175
00:27:39,400 --> 00:27:42,280
Attacking is better than waiting for them.

176
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:45,860
However, we are not strong enough to
attack them right now.

177
00:27:45,860 --> 00:27:48,460
Not all Beys are present at the moment.

178
00:27:49,220 --> 00:27:56,440
If all of them were present, I'd tell you
to arm ourselves and combine our power...

179
00:27:56,520 --> 00:27:59,400
... to destroy the army of Geyhatu.

180
00:28:02,180 --> 00:28:07,680
This is the sole reason why I'm suggesting
breaking the wings of his supporters.

181
00:28:10,020 --> 00:28:15,040
I suggest we kill the soldiers and
commanders of Mongols...

182
00:28:15,140 --> 00:28:20,760
... who walk between the confidentials
and sacreds of our people.

183
00:28:22,580 --> 00:28:27,820
To achieve this, we shall form an
Akıncı Troop with high tier Alps.

184
00:28:27,860 --> 00:28:31,060
They shall be Valiant muslims.

185
00:28:32,780 --> 00:28:37,540
These Valiants who will come from the
muslim regions...

186
00:28:37,800 --> 00:28:40,800
... shall kill the best soldiers the
Mongols have.

187
00:28:41,140 --> 00:28:45,540
In the end, the Mongols will never have
the time to rest.

188
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:49,700
When did you come up this plan, Osman
Bey?

189
00:28:50,360 --> 00:28:53,440
You are dreaming of conquest non-stop.

190
00:28:53,500 --> 00:28:57,000
That's not the case at all.

191
00:28:58,360 --> 00:29:02,960
We are the community of our prophet.

192
00:29:05,040 --> 00:29:07,560
What did our highness order?

193
00:29:07,840 --> 00:29:11,520
To live the same day twice is a waste.

194
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:18,720
For that reason, we'll fight,
we'll dream...

195
00:29:18,720 --> 00:29:22,880
... we'll struggle,
we'll trade.

196
00:29:23,560 --> 00:29:27,280
And we will chat.

197
00:29:27,440 --> 00:29:32,400
But our two days won't be the same.

198
00:29:33,720 --> 00:29:38,400
An Islamic union with valiants
who swore for shahada...

199
00:29:38,400 --> 00:29:44,000
... a group of man who swore
to destroy the enemy.

200
00:29:44,840 --> 00:29:47,400
Isn't this the whole story?

201
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:50,840
Aren't a group of people enough?

202
00:29:50,840 --> 00:29:55,560
How many of us were there in the battle
of Badr? In the battle of Uhud?

203
00:29:55,840 --> 00:29:58,960
How many of us were there in
the conquest of Mecca?

204
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:03,640
Were we not a handful
in many other battles?

205
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:07,040
May I enter, my Bey?

206
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:10,240
Come in, Saltuk.

207
00:30:15,120 --> 00:30:20,400
News, my Bey. Surrounding areas' Lords
will come together in İnegöl.

208
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:24,000
Nikola is preparing for a new crusade.

209
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:30,840
They want revenge, Osman Bey.

210
00:30:33,440 --> 00:30:38,000
- Tell the Alps to prepare.
- As you order, my Bey.

211
00:30:43,560 --> 00:30:45,840
Do you need support?

212
00:30:49,800 --> 00:30:51,600
Your prayers are enough.

213
00:30:51,600 --> 00:30:56,800
Our prayers are with you.
Our cause is big, our paths are long.

214
00:30:56,800 --> 00:30:58,680
More effort is what we need.

215
00:30:58,680 --> 00:31:03,280
Our hearts are big, our
brotherhood is eternal.

216
00:31:04,280 --> 00:31:07,400
- Give us your blessings.
- Bless you.

217
00:31:42,480 --> 00:31:46,480
Losing this battle does not
mean losing the war.

218
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:52,440
For example, every defeat is
another whip. More and even more!

219
00:31:55,920 --> 00:31:58,040
Were you like this, mighty Ceasar?

220
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:04,520
That’s what I thought.

221
00:32:37,960 --> 00:32:40,400
Antandros!

222
00:32:40,400 --> 00:32:44,400
How’s your daughter?
She was ill. Is she okay?

223
00:32:45,800 --> 00:32:48,240
Mighty Ceasar blessed my daughter.

224
00:32:52,440 --> 00:32:54,200
Nikis!

225
00:32:56,960 --> 00:33:00,320
Your wife knows
you’re cheating on her.

226
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:10,920
Here’s an advice.
Fear a lover’s anger.

227
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:16,600
How do you know that?

228
00:33:19,480 --> 00:33:26,000
With the wife of your
closest commander. Is that it?

229
00:33:28,440 --> 00:33:36,600
Be cautious of the pain of the dagger you
will have on your back once the time comes.

230
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:41,920
And, Pakimeres!

231
00:33:49,400 --> 00:33:56,480
So, Pakimeres, were the trade deals you
made with the Turks enough for you?

232
00:33:56,480 --> 00:34:00,960
As you know, trade and
war are separate, Nikola.

233
00:34:04,160 --> 00:34:11,880
Osman, killed all the soldiers
our Empire sent their way.

234
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:16,960
He also wounded my friend Alexander.

235
00:34:19,280 --> 00:34:22,280
Let me ask you a question, Pakimeres.

236
00:34:22,280 --> 00:34:24,719
If it goes on likes this…

237
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:34,320
… can Osman also take your
heads and your castles?

238
00:34:34,880 --> 00:34:36,800
Tell me.

239
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:41,080
Tell me!

240
00:34:41,080 --> 00:34:45,639
- You’re right, Nikola.
- I couldn’t hear you.

241
00:34:45,639 --> 00:34:48,480
We’re here to obey your orders.

242
00:34:53,560 --> 00:34:55,800
Good.

243
00:34:57,080 --> 00:35:02,040
Men! The dirty part of politics is over.

244
00:35:02,760 --> 00:35:06,040
Poisonous power of the gold is also over.

245
00:35:07,800 --> 00:35:12,160
There is one power now.
The power of battle!

246
00:35:12,160 --> 00:35:15,200
The power of battling to death!

247
00:35:25,600 --> 00:35:27,520
To death.

248
00:35:40,800 --> 00:35:47,640
Osman Bey. Hatuns of Kayı made
it with passion and love.

249
00:36:00,520 --> 00:36:02,920
Thank them.

250
00:36:05,960 --> 00:36:07,560
How is it, Boran?

251
00:36:08,400 --> 00:36:11,200
What is it for, my Bey?

252
00:36:11,200 --> 00:36:13,840
The new banner of Kayı.

253
00:36:17,520 --> 00:36:19,280
Crescent and arrow.

254
00:36:19,280 --> 00:36:21,640
Symbol of the world’s order.

255
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:26,840
It shows the Turks’ way of battle.

256
00:36:29,600 --> 00:36:32,360
The banner of resurrection.

257
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:40,800
Announcement of the new state
we will establish to the whole world.

258
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:48,120
Thank you, Osman Bey.
May my Allah bless it.

259
00:36:48,120 --> 00:36:52,760
May our Tent be a beylic,
may our beylic be a state.

260
00:36:53,960 --> 00:36:56,240
May our state be blessed, my Bey.

261
00:36:56,240 --> 00:36:58,200
Inshallah!

262
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:03,680
Kulacahisar veteran Aygül Hatun.

263
00:37:04,560 --> 00:37:08,280
Now, she'll be
the head of the women’s union.

264
00:37:10,640 --> 00:37:12,880
May Allah bless it.

265
00:37:21,560 --> 00:37:27,840
Osman Bey, you saw me fit, and
that made me happy.

266
00:37:28,720 --> 00:37:33,000
You gave me a duty, and I’m proud of it.

267
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:37,920
We're always there with our
swords whenever you need us.

268
00:37:37,920 --> 00:37:43,160
We’ll hit the enemy's armies
like the lionesses that we are!

269
00:37:48,320 --> 00:37:49,960
Thank you.

270
00:37:57,840 --> 00:38:00,160
A great duty awaits.

271
00:38:01,840 --> 00:38:07,720
Being brave and strong aren't
enough, you need to be cautious.

272
00:38:09,240 --> 00:38:14,520
You’ll be cautious.
You'll take care of each other.

273
00:38:15,600 --> 00:38:19,960
Don’t you make a mistake.

274
00:38:19,960 --> 00:38:22,560
Don’t worry, my Bey.

275
00:38:23,040 --> 00:38:24,600
Boran!

276
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:29,200
You’re in charge.

277
00:38:29,720 --> 00:38:31,120
As you order my Bey.

278
00:38:31,120 --> 00:38:33,040
As for the duty…

279
00:38:35,720 --> 00:38:39,840
- You’ll infiltrate İnegöl.
- As you order, my Bey.

280
00:38:39,840 --> 00:38:43,320
Nikola is serving
a feast for the Lords.

281
00:38:43,320 --> 00:38:48,440
He gathered all
the Lords for a big crusade.

282
00:38:48,440 --> 00:38:52,320
Infidel! He doesn’t behave himself.

283
00:38:52,320 --> 00:38:56,320
A dog is always a dog, brother.

284
00:38:56,320 --> 00:38:59,040
How will we do that, my Bey?

285
00:38:59,040 --> 00:39:02,200
Do you know Sarı Saltuk?

286
00:39:02,200 --> 00:39:06,480
My Bey! How does a
valiant doesn’t know Sarı Saltuk?

287
00:39:09,200 --> 00:39:16,800
You’ll enter the enemy's
lair with any tricks necessary.

288
00:39:17,960 --> 00:39:23,600
My Alps! I want you
to decide for yourself.

289
00:39:24,400 --> 00:39:27,000
I want you to think for yourself.

290
00:39:28,360 --> 00:39:33,440
Because those who grow
a state, are the mature ones.

291
00:39:35,040 --> 00:39:41,800
Once our army is huge, I want
the mature ones leading it!

292
00:39:42,960 --> 00:39:46,760
For this reason, the duty is yours.

293
00:39:47,440 --> 00:39:53,800
Prepare the operation.
And don’t embarrass me.

294
00:39:54,720 --> 00:40:00,440
Don’t worry, my Bey.
We’ll strangle them in their own castles.

295
00:40:00,440 --> 00:40:09,320
We must make our enemy understand that
they can’t even imagine beating us!

296
00:40:09,320 --> 00:40:19,480
If you even try, then
we’ll take that mind out of your heads!

297
00:40:22,040 --> 00:40:28,200
My Bey! We can enter it. But…

298
00:40:30,640 --> 00:40:33,560
How will we exit, my Bey?

299
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:53,560
If you can’t,
you’ll be prisoners.

300
00:40:56,280 --> 00:40:59,440
And you’ll get
a taste of shahada.

301
00:41:01,240 --> 00:41:03,040
Thank you, my Bey.

302
00:41:07,120 --> 00:41:12,040
The job is ours, my Bey.
Don’t worry.

303
00:41:18,440 --> 00:41:24,600
Brothers! You may
not come back from this duty.

304
00:41:25,760 --> 00:41:29,320
- Give your blessings.
- Bless you, my Bey.

305
00:41:30,760 --> 00:41:36,680
Brothers!

306
00:41:59,120 --> 00:42:04,400
My Bey.
Being a martyr is an honour.

307
00:42:06,200 --> 00:42:11,480
But if we become prisoners,
we might never see you again.

308
00:42:30,920 --> 00:42:35,080
We used to be like that
when we were young, Osman Bey.

309
00:42:36,560 --> 00:42:39,280
You’re not old yet,
Abdurrahman Gazi.

310
00:42:40,200 --> 00:42:46,520
I still need you.
No one else can do this.

311
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:53,160
No one will know where you
will go and what you will do.

312
00:42:54,120 --> 00:42:57,960
Your secret is my secret, my Bey.

313
00:43:00,080 --> 00:43:02,400
Thank you.

314
00:43:04,960 --> 00:43:10,040
Abdurrahman Gazi!
We always need to be one stop ahead.

315
00:43:15,080 --> 00:43:19,560
- May Allah Bless you.
- Bless you.

316
00:43:20,200 --> 00:43:23,280
May Allah bless both Osman Bey and you.

317
00:43:23,280 --> 00:43:25,840
May Allah bless you too.

318
00:43:37,280 --> 00:43:39,040
Welcome, sister.

319
00:43:39,040 --> 00:43:42,000
- Allah bless you.
- Enjoy your meal.

320
00:43:42,000 --> 00:43:45,520
- May my Allah bless you!
- Thank you!

321
00:43:46,480 --> 00:43:48,400
Mother!

322
00:43:51,600 --> 00:43:55,120
- May Allah always be with you!
- Mother, wait!

323
00:43:55,120 --> 00:43:58,240
Hafza Hatun! Please take care of this.

324
00:43:59,960 --> 00:44:01,960
Come, mother.

325
00:44:07,280 --> 00:44:09,800
Hand me the basket, sister.

326
00:44:18,440 --> 00:44:21,840
May God protect you and
Osman Bey, Bala Hatun!

327
00:44:21,840 --> 00:44:24,040
Amen, mother.

328
00:44:46,520 --> 00:44:52,240
Mother. Take these so
you can cook at home.

329
00:44:52,240 --> 00:44:54,480
May God help you.

330
00:44:56,320 --> 00:44:59,720
- Wait. Yusuf Alp!
- Yes, Bala Hatun?

331
00:44:59,720 --> 00:45:02,880
Help this lady take her supplies home.

332
00:45:02,880 --> 00:45:05,720
- As you order, Bala Hatun.
- Thank you.

333
00:45:05,720 --> 00:45:09,120
- I’ll get it.
- Thank you, mother.

334
00:45:16,120 --> 00:45:21,920
Bala. Bala Sultan!
How nice of you!

335
00:45:23,080 --> 00:45:27,000
Thanks to you, so
many people are fed.

336
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:31,360
Don’t say that, my Gonca.
Allah is the one who gives.

337
00:45:31,360 --> 00:45:34,200
That’s my sister with a clean heart!

338
00:45:34,200 --> 00:45:39,880
If my Sheikh saw
your efforts, he’d be so happy.

339
00:45:44,440 --> 00:45:48,120
The father is a strong castle for a girl.

340
00:45:49,240 --> 00:45:53,200
Oh how much I need him
during troubling times.

341
00:45:54,400 --> 00:45:58,600
I can’t wait for him to
come back from hajj!

342
00:45:58,600 --> 00:46:00,480
Inshallah, my Bala.

343
00:46:22,000 --> 00:46:27,840
Father. I’m sad that my
mother still won’t talk to me.

344
00:46:32,400 --> 00:46:34,920
Can you turn dough into wheat?

345
00:46:34,920 --> 00:46:37,720
It doesn’t, but…

346
00:46:38,920 --> 00:46:41,760
I know that just like every Turk…

347
00:46:41,840 --> 00:46:46,320
… the sound of swords clashing
and horses running gets you excited.

348
00:46:46,320 --> 00:46:50,720
But you weren't
raised to be an Alp.

349
00:46:53,600 --> 00:46:57,560
Remember that these
lands also need wise men.

350
00:46:57,560 --> 00:47:02,480
Besides, was all your
education for nothing?

351
00:47:02,480 --> 00:47:05,280
Did you read that
many books for nothing?

352
00:47:05,280 --> 00:47:09,760
Father! Can't one be both
an intellect and a warrior?

353
00:47:10,720 --> 00:47:13,880
Of course one can.

354
00:47:15,440 --> 00:47:19,480
But now, we need
intellects more.

355
00:47:20,640 --> 00:47:25,760
Also, you haven't made
use of your education yet.

356
00:47:26,960 --> 00:47:33,360
Yes, you have to.
This is where you will.

357
00:47:39,240 --> 00:47:46,120
Remember. States are
found by the efforts of veterans.

358
00:47:46,120 --> 00:47:51,080
But they survive
under the intellects’ lights.

359
00:47:51,800 --> 00:47:53,640
Thank you.

360
00:47:54,480 --> 00:47:56,800
Let’s go.

361
00:48:55,040 --> 00:49:00,720
Brother! Osman Bey is giving
us duties so we can gain experience.

362
00:49:00,720 --> 00:49:02,320
Look at what you do…

363
00:49:02,320 --> 00:49:07,160
What did I do, Boran?
Can’t we ask questions to our Bey?

364
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:13,240
Brother. Where did
you grow that head of yours?

365
00:49:17,600 --> 00:49:20,360
Let’s go, brothers.

366
00:49:34,640 --> 00:49:36,520
Boran Alp!

367
00:49:38,000 --> 00:49:39,960
Where do you go to?

368
00:49:42,080 --> 00:49:47,000
- To hunt.
- Did Osman Bey give you news orders?

369
00:49:50,840 --> 00:49:53,160
What are you talking about?

370
00:49:57,400 --> 00:50:01,000
Boran Alp.
This hunt looks different.

371
00:50:03,480 --> 00:50:08,760
That Boy will get himself into
trouble again. My God, protect him.

372
00:50:09,800 --> 00:50:18,000
I said we’re going to hunt. No more
questions. We've got places to be.

373
00:50:19,800 --> 00:50:23,200
So be it. Go.

374
00:50:24,320 --> 00:50:27,960
Let’s go, brothers!

375
00:50:34,440 --> 00:50:37,240
I won’t leave
you alone with this hunt.

376
00:50:54,040 --> 00:50:56,080
Bayhoca!

377
00:51:03,720 --> 00:51:08,160
Bayhoca!

378
00:51:16,880 --> 00:51:19,520
He never listens!

379
00:51:19,520 --> 00:51:23,280
Oh, Bayhoca!

380
00:51:39,600 --> 00:51:46,360
Praise be!

381
00:51:47,320 --> 00:51:55,120
Bala, my daughter. You called me
to help you for such a good cause.

382
00:51:55,120 --> 00:51:58,240
Thank you, daughter.
It made me very happy.

383
00:51:58,240 --> 00:52:02,640
Teamwork makes the dream
work, Hazal Hatun. Thank you.

384
00:52:02,640 --> 00:52:09,000
But, just supporting
isn’t enough. I want you to help.

385
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:13,240
Of course I will!
As long as you want it.

386
00:52:13,240 --> 00:52:16,640
Come on, Alps!
Take the goods down.

387
00:52:25,120 --> 00:52:27,280
Thank you.

388
00:52:35,000 --> 00:52:38,880
Bala Hatun!
May I?

389
00:52:41,000 --> 00:52:43,440
Sure, Hatun.

390
00:52:44,080 --> 00:52:48,320
I’ve heard that you
were helping the poor, Bala Hatun.

391
00:52:50,120 --> 00:52:53,480
I brought some from
the supplies in my house.

392
00:52:53,480 --> 00:52:56,240
If you allow me, I’d
like to hand them away.

393
00:52:58,160 --> 00:53:03,880
Thank you, my beautiful
sister. Here, bring them in.

394
00:53:08,560 --> 00:53:14,880
Praise be, Bala. More
and more people are coming to help.

395
00:53:17,680 --> 00:53:20,240
Praise be.

396
00:53:36,760 --> 00:53:38,320
Bala?

397
00:53:39,920 --> 00:53:42,120
Are you okay?

398
00:53:45,800 --> 00:53:49,480
I need to find a second
Hatun for Osman Bey, Gonca.

399
00:53:50,400 --> 00:53:52,360
This topic again...

400
00:53:53,000 --> 00:53:55,600
It's not about Osman
or me anymore.

401
00:53:57,120 --> 00:53:59,400
It's the will of Ertuğrul Gazi.

402
00:53:59,400 --> 00:54:01,480
What are you saying, Bala?

403
00:54:02,920 --> 00:54:05,920
There can be no Bey
without a child, Gonca.

404
00:54:07,960 --> 00:54:10,560
That's why I need to find it.

405
00:54:18,480 --> 00:54:25,000
Bala Hatun, if you allow
me, I'd like to help.

406
00:54:42,080 --> 00:54:48,760
To escape the Mongol's taxes,
the Turks sell their goods to you.

407
00:54:51,080 --> 00:54:54,400
So, they can survive
thanks to you.

408
00:54:55,400 --> 00:54:59,920
You're the reason new Tents
attack us with new Alps.

409
00:55:01,200 --> 00:55:04,640
There are three paths they can
sell their good through.

410
00:55:04,640 --> 00:55:09,280
Bursa, İnegöl, Constantinople.

411
00:55:09,920 --> 00:55:13,400
All three of these roads
will be closed.

412
00:55:14,920 --> 00:55:18,040
With your soldiers, not
only the traders...

413
00:55:18,040 --> 00:55:24,200
... but also the shepherds,
the Turks in your bazaars...

414
00:55:24,200 --> 00:55:27,000
You will hunt them down one by one.

415
00:55:27,960 --> 00:55:34,160
If you forget that they need
to die because they are Turks...

416
00:55:34,440 --> 00:55:39,280
I'll forget that you are Lords.

417
00:55:41,040 --> 00:55:45,640
You know what comes after this.
War.

418
00:55:45,640 --> 00:55:52,520
Not just war.
Blood, tears, and booty.

419
00:55:55,480 --> 00:56:03,280
Men! All the booty you take will be yours
free of the Empire's tax.

420
00:56:03,280 --> 00:56:06,240
You'll attack Osman
from three sides.

421
00:56:06,240 --> 00:56:09,960
Until he can't breathe.

422
00:56:10,960 --> 00:56:13,240
What happens when they
start attacking?

423
00:56:13,240 --> 00:56:14,840
What happens?

424
00:56:15,880 --> 00:56:22,240
You just close your castles' doors.
The rest...

425
00:56:23,720 --> 00:56:25,560
... is my job.

426
00:56:25,840 --> 00:56:30,280
I'll be with you with an army
larger than ever before.

427
00:56:30,320 --> 00:56:32,800
Not just the Empire's army.

428
00:56:32,800 --> 00:56:38,560
I'll crush them with an army
of Mongols and Cumans!

429
00:56:40,320 --> 00:56:43,640
Any objections?

430
00:56:46,400 --> 00:56:50,240
Good.
Then...

431
00:56:53,320 --> 00:56:58,640
- Battle to death!
-Battle to death!

432
00:57:04,280 --> 00:57:08,560
Good. Finally, we've
come to the point.

433
00:57:09,120 --> 00:57:12,520
I like battling to death.

434
00:57:13,280 --> 00:57:17,360
Men. You're my
guests for the night.

435
00:57:17,360 --> 00:57:26,400
And remember. I don't consider you Lords
until you give me a tasbih made of Turks.

436
00:57:31,960 --> 00:57:33,800
For Rome!

437
00:58:48,116 --> 00:58:51,466
Who are you?

438
00:59:09,145 --> 00:59:11,805
Get off the cart!

439
00:59:14,052 --> 00:59:17,652
I beg you, don't kill us!

440
01:00:04,755 --> 01:00:08,755
Help us! Isn't there anyone!

441
01:00:08,755 --> 01:00:12,755
Help us!
Help us!

442
01:00:14,532 --> 01:00:18,532
-Help us!
-Help us!

443
01:00:24,215 --> 01:00:28,215
Boran, sing us something.

444
01:00:28,475 --> 01:00:32,475
Don't talk, just fight.

445
01:00:36,385 --> 01:00:39,595
Isn't there anyone?

446
01:00:41,103 --> 01:00:46,113
Help us! Help us, I beg you!
Help us!

447
01:00:51,976 --> 01:00:56,256
-Who are you?
-We are poor musicians, sir.

448
01:00:56,256 --> 01:01:01,366
We were going to Tekfur Nikola's
feast. Three Turks stopped us...

449
01:01:01,774 --> 01:01:06,454
...they took our clothes
and instruments. Please, help us.

450
01:02:02,244 --> 01:02:09,254
Put it there. Get the oil and
carry it there. Good.

451
01:02:34,115 --> 01:02:40,585
-What's your name, woman?
-My name is Aksu. I live in Söğüt.

452
01:02:42,864 --> 01:02:46,864
-Which family?
-My father is a trader.

453
01:02:46,864 --> 01:02:52,974
We lost him early. We live with
what he has left.

454
01:02:52,974 --> 01:02:58,244
-My mother and I live on our own.
-Mashallah.

455
01:03:08,454 --> 01:03:12,454
Don't you have anyone else?

456
01:03:13,110 --> 01:03:16,130
We don't, my lady.

457
01:03:18,861 --> 01:03:23,851
With this beauty, why didn't you
marry already?

458
01:03:25,303 --> 01:03:30,193
There were candidates...

459
01:03:30,460 --> 01:03:34,460
...but let's say it was Allah's
decision.

460
01:03:38,415 --> 01:03:41,405
There is goodness in everything.

461
01:03:45,585 --> 01:03:49,585
Maybe fate will smile upon you.

462
01:04:13,184 --> 01:04:17,184
I knew you would come, Aksu.

463
01:04:17,672 --> 01:04:19,972
Come.

464
01:04:22,314 --> 01:04:26,314
Have your family received
their every need?

465
01:04:26,514 --> 01:04:30,834
-They have, my lady. Thank you.
-Not at all.

466
01:04:31,286 --> 01:04:33,476
Thank you too.

467
01:04:44,641 --> 01:04:47,141
Mashallah.

468
01:04:48,019 --> 01:04:51,279
It fits you so well.

469
01:04:53,237 --> 01:04:59,857
These are the gold coins
I mentioned you.

470
01:05:10,835 --> 01:05:14,675
But my lady, what do you
want from me?

471
01:05:14,675 --> 01:05:16,365
Aksu.

472
01:05:18,087 --> 01:05:22,897
My pretty daughter,
from now on...

473
01:05:22,897 --> 01:05:27,287
...you will be like my daughter.

474
01:05:28,834 --> 01:05:36,524
But at first, no one will know this.

475
01:05:40,501 --> 01:05:47,551
I will find you a good spouse.

476
01:05:49,334 --> 01:05:55,294
But only if you do everything
as I say.

477
01:05:55,294 --> 01:06:01,144
I owe you my life, my lady.
Order me to die and I will.

478
01:06:03,397 --> 01:06:07,937
All right. I will make you...

479
01:06:08,126 --> 01:06:10,576
...Osman's...

480
01:06:12,215 --> 01:06:17,775
...Osman Bey's wife.

481
01:06:29,079 --> 01:06:33,469
But there is an...

482
01:06:33,560 --> 01:06:38,140
...al-Sirat bridge that you need
to pass.

483
01:07:02,928 --> 01:07:06,928
So, Bala Hatun.
Thank Allah.

484
01:07:06,928 --> 01:07:10,928
-I finished my job.
-Thank you, Hazal Hatun.

485
01:07:10,928 --> 01:07:16,928
-I appreciate your help here.
-Of course, I will help you.

486
01:07:27,155 --> 01:07:31,155
But you look sad?

487
01:07:32,270 --> 01:07:37,760
Is there a person free of sadness?
We can talk later.

488
01:07:38,731 --> 01:07:45,181
Of course, but don't endure
in silence, my daughter.

489
01:07:47,978 --> 01:07:51,978
Hazal Hatun is always with you.

490
01:07:52,680 --> 01:07:56,200
Thank you.

491
01:08:53,364 --> 01:08:57,364
What's wrong, Cerkutay?
Is something up?

492
01:08:58,073 --> 01:09:01,773
-My bey, am I not a warrior?
-You are, Cerkutay.

493
01:09:01,867 --> 01:09:06,441
-Then why doesn't Osman Bey call me?
-He awaits me to name you ready.

494
01:09:06,441 --> 01:09:10,631
My bey, what are you waiting for?

495
01:09:11,658 --> 01:09:16,828
Cerkutay, do you remember the
words I taught you?

496
01:09:17,426 --> 01:09:19,536
In my head--

497
01:09:22,534 --> 01:09:25,084
In my heart.

498
01:09:25,537 --> 01:09:29,537
If they are in your heart, repeat them.

499
01:09:30,752 --> 01:09:36,102
I will control my hand, my tongue
and my waist.

500
01:09:36,684 --> 01:09:41,194
I won't strike someone who yield...

501
01:09:41,194 --> 01:09:46,204
...I won't pull my sword against women,
children and helpless. I know the rest.

502
01:09:46,204 --> 01:09:47,784
I won't step back from a battle.

503
01:10:07,946 --> 01:10:12,646
What's wrong, İdris Bey?
What are you looking at?

504
01:10:12,789 --> 01:10:16,789
Doesn't your arm work anymore, Bamsı Bey?

505
01:10:21,101 --> 01:10:23,431
İdris Bey.

506
01:10:24,515 --> 01:10:27,305
İdris Bey!

507
01:10:38,370 --> 01:10:43,603
Come on, alps, come on!
Be quick!

508
01:10:49,144 --> 01:10:54,681
-We'll hang them in Kulucahisar and Söğüt too.
-Move aside!

509
01:11:11,328 --> 01:11:18,076
My Allah! My Allah!
What is this? What is this?

510
01:11:18,255 --> 01:11:19,255
What is this?

511
01:11:19,571 --> 01:11:22,011
Hold on, uncle.
We'll find out.

512
01:11:22,011 --> 01:11:26,821
Davud Bey!
Davud Bey!

513
01:11:28,289 --> 01:11:34,129
What is this? What is this?
Where are our flags!

514
01:11:35,027 --> 01:11:38,537
Our flags are here, Bamsı Bey.

515
01:11:44,256 --> 01:11:48,616
-Did Osman Bey order this?
-Osman Bey ordered this.

516
01:11:48,616 --> 01:11:52,616
-What kind of a thing is this?
-His tent is right there.

517
01:11:53,510 --> 01:11:56,000
Go on.

518
01:11:56,617 --> 01:11:58,137
Come on.

519
01:12:06,560 --> 01:12:09,830
Open the doors!

520
01:12:09,968 --> 01:12:12,598
Osman Bey.

521
01:12:15,532 --> 01:12:18,292
Osman Bey!

522
01:12:20,335 --> 01:12:25,915
Those flags... Our flag...
Why did they change?

523
01:12:26,659 --> 01:12:31,849
Who did you talk to before
making such a decision?

524
01:12:31,849 --> 01:12:36,729
No one! And the beys
don't allow it!

525
01:12:39,453 --> 01:12:44,763
We came all this way under
that blue banners!

526
01:12:45,504 --> 01:12:50,654
We found peace under its shadow,
we had dreams.

527
01:12:52,072 --> 01:12:54,882
Now you can't change it, Osman Bey!

528
01:12:54,882 --> 01:12:59,172
This flag is our common value.
You can't change it!

529
01:12:59,969 --> 01:13:06,029
You should lower it at once. Or else
neither our beylig or your throne will stand.

530
01:13:21,209 --> 01:13:27,149
I see that my beys are disturbed
by my actions.

531
01:13:29,591 --> 01:13:31,721
I heard that...

532
01:13:33,508 --> 01:13:37,068
...my position is threatened.

533
01:13:54,157 --> 01:13:59,847
Under this holy flag, Kayı people
found peace.

534
01:14:01,666 --> 01:14:05,666
They fought, it's true.

535
01:14:21,028 --> 01:14:25,998
Dodurga Tribe also flies its own banner.

536
01:14:25,998 --> 01:14:29,998
Salur Tribe also flies its own banner.

537
01:14:30,244 --> 01:14:36,904
My ancestor Oghuz has 24 tribes.
And they all have marks.

538
01:14:37,490 --> 01:14:41,490
Every tribe dreams for its own.

539
01:14:41,490 --> 01:14:45,790
And every tribe builds its own
order.

540
01:14:45,928 --> 01:14:54,878
Then, who will unite the separated
tribes of Oghuz Khan?

541
01:14:55,008 --> 01:15:00,428
Who will bring them together?
Who will realize our dreams?

542
01:15:00,860 --> 01:15:07,680
Who will say that we are brothers,
that we are of the same blood?

543
01:15:08,934 --> 01:15:11,524
Who?

544
01:15:13,183 --> 01:15:18,193
We will.
We will!

545
01:15:19,958 --> 01:15:22,858
We will!

546
01:15:24,700 --> 01:15:28,700
Osman Bey, we...

547
01:15:28,717 --> 01:15:33,907
...are used to living under that
sky blue banner.

548
01:15:36,963 --> 01:15:40,963
That flag is the legacy
of our ancestors.

549
01:15:41,038 --> 01:15:46,768
This flag is the symbol of resistance
and resurrection.

550
01:15:47,586 --> 01:15:52,106
We resisted with this flag and
we resurrected.

551
01:15:54,455 --> 01:15:58,455
Now, we are on our feet.

552
01:15:58,455 --> 01:16:02,455
Now, we will walk.

553
01:16:03,876 --> 01:16:09,616
Now is the time of jihad.
Now is the time of the conquest.

554
01:16:17,481 --> 01:16:22,201
Now, I will ask you a question.

555
01:16:24,427 --> 01:16:28,427
What will destroy the Islam world?

556
01:16:30,688 --> 01:16:34,688
Separation.
Disagreement.

557
01:16:35,929 --> 01:16:40,919
Unrest. Laziness.

558
01:16:42,463 --> 01:16:51,303
For this reason, I offer you to
unite all tribes under one crescent.

559
01:16:52,615 --> 01:16:56,615
This is such a great
crescent that...

560
01:16:56,615 --> 01:17:00,615
...the shadow of that crescent...

561
01:17:01,569 --> 01:17:04,999
...will cover all the world.

562
01:17:16,374 --> 01:17:21,494
Without discriminating the tribes,
we'll form a great state.

563
01:17:22,679 --> 01:17:29,379
This country isn't only the country of
the Kayı but all the Turks.

564
01:17:29,997 --> 01:17:35,227
It will be the country of the Islam world.
It will be the country of the oppressed.

565
01:17:37,291 --> 01:17:45,611
Under this crescent, 7 regions and
72 nation will find peace.

566
01:17:59,958 --> 01:18:04,388
All right, Osman Bey.

567
01:18:14,191 --> 01:18:19,831
You are right.
You thought well.

568
01:18:20,456 --> 01:18:26,916
But, Osman Bey, great dreams
end with sorrow...

569
01:18:26,916 --> 01:18:29,096
...if they aren't talked about.

570
01:18:35,010 --> 01:18:40,770
Now, if you don't include
us to your great dreams...

571
01:18:43,464 --> 01:18:48,984
...you can't create a country
or do conquests.

572
01:19:08,440 --> 01:19:11,830
Forgive me.

573
01:19:13,611 --> 01:19:17,611
As long as I have valiants
who speak the truth, as you...

574
01:19:19,964 --> 01:19:25,724
...no one can beat us.

575
01:19:33,959 --> 01:19:37,109
Brother.

576
01:19:39,477 --> 01:19:44,707
The sharpness of your mind made me glad.
Long you live, Osman Bey.

577
01:19:50,077 --> 01:19:54,077
Long you live, Osman Bey.

578
01:19:54,698 --> 01:19:58,698
You didn't ashame...

579
01:19:59,901 --> 01:20:03,231
...my Ertuğrul Ghazi.

580
01:20:06,444 --> 01:20:11,104
Long you live, Osman Bey.

581
01:20:18,458 --> 01:20:22,908
Long you live, Osman Bey.
Long you live.

582
01:20:25,212 --> 01:20:29,212
Long you live.

583
01:20:29,212 --> 01:20:33,512
If you get disturbed by a decision
I make again, one day...

584
01:20:34,344 --> 01:20:38,344
...don't give up on what you believe in.

585
01:20:39,005 --> 01:20:43,005
After all, this tent will
be...

586
01:20:43,041 --> 01:20:48,351
...the home of heart and mind.

587
01:21:00,830 --> 01:21:03,220
Bamsı Bey.

588
01:22:10,801 --> 01:22:15,831
Where do the most beautiful women
of Bithynia live in? İnegöl!

589
01:22:18,577 --> 01:22:24,367
Where does the greatest commander of
Rome live in? İnegöl!

590
01:22:26,271 --> 01:22:30,631
Play for Lord Nikola!

591
01:22:46,010 --> 01:22:51,260
-Speak of the devil...
-Stay calm, friends.

592
01:22:56,300 --> 01:23:00,300
Heroic commanders of Bithynia!

593
01:23:00,437 --> 01:23:04,937
Where were you all this time?
We were expecting you earlier.

594
01:23:32,784 --> 01:23:37,264
We came to turn our voice and
instruments into gold, sir.

595
01:23:38,181 --> 01:23:42,341
If you are late, you should
entertain us first.

596
01:23:42,710 --> 01:23:46,870
Tell me, my noble commander.
What's the name of your beloved one?

597
01:23:47,101 --> 01:23:53,031
-Helena.
-Helena? Helena.

598
01:23:55,165 --> 01:23:57,605
Helena...

599
01:24:08,231 --> 01:24:12,231
Helena...
Helena...

600
01:24:15,403 --> 01:24:17,434
Helena...

601
01:24:26,367 --> 01:24:33,034
Helena...
Helena...

602
01:24:35,934 --> 01:24:40,234
Save me from this pain...

603
01:24:40,507 --> 01:24:44,507
...I will die from my love!

604
01:24:44,687 --> 01:24:48,687
Helena...

605
01:24:51,249 --> 01:24:53,959
Helena!

606
01:25:02,523 --> 01:25:06,523
Helena...
Helena...

607
01:25:07,802 --> 01:25:11,802
Ohh, Helena...

608
01:25:16,144 --> 01:25:20,144
I will come to your show
without coins.

609
01:25:21,058 --> 01:25:26,238
Our show is our gift
to all the soldiers of the castle!

610
01:26:17,418 --> 01:26:21,148
I guess you are lost in the castle.

611
01:26:21,148 --> 01:26:24,828
I'm sure someone will give us a hand.

612
01:26:35,554 --> 01:26:40,284
A room is prepared for the musicians.
Zülfikar will get you at night.

613
01:26:40,284 --> 01:26:42,774
Now go to your room and wait.

614
01:26:46,275 --> 01:26:48,525
-Boran Alp.
-Yeah?

615
01:26:48,525 --> 01:26:53,145
Look at this? Our bey's spy
in the castle is a young girl.

616
01:27:04,392 --> 01:27:07,792
It's me, Bayhoca.

617
01:27:08,899 --> 01:27:12,329
-Bayhoca?
-What are you doing here?

618
01:27:12,329 --> 01:27:15,939
I thought you would need me.

619
01:27:21,430 --> 01:27:25,830
Oh, my dear friend! You are late.
We were waiting for you!

620
01:27:29,896 --> 01:27:34,686
If you weren't Savcı Bey's son,
I would hang you here, Bayhoca.

621
01:27:34,686 --> 01:27:39,006
-But I--
-My bey, when will you grow up?

622
01:27:39,601 --> 01:27:43,191
Brother Boran, what will we do now?

623
01:27:43,191 --> 01:27:47,191
-I want to throw him over the walls but...
-But I--

624
01:27:47,191 --> 01:27:50,191
Silence. Silence. Don't talk.

625
01:27:50,951 --> 01:27:54,951
Such a trouble-maker...

626
01:27:54,951 --> 01:28:01,241
Pray to Allah that you carry Osman Bey's
blood. We have to protect him now.

627
01:28:21,433 --> 01:28:28,113
To be honest, I admire your talent, sir.

628
01:28:28,230 --> 01:28:33,760
We were raised by the holy pope,
'brother'.

629
01:28:35,674 --> 01:28:42,314
His holy hands can disguise us in
any shape, 'thank Allah'.

630
01:28:44,688 --> 01:28:50,028
But if we can't access the information
that Bamsı hides...

631
01:28:50,219 --> 01:28:55,149
...his holy hands will introduce
us to death.

632
01:28:56,794 --> 01:29:00,994
David is in the tribe. He is tracing.

633
01:29:00,994 --> 01:29:06,514
He is after Bamsı. And after our last
blow...

634
01:29:07,140 --> 01:29:11,600
...Bamsı lost all his power.

635
01:29:19,056 --> 01:29:26,076
If needed, we'll organize a night
operation.

636
01:29:26,303 --> 01:29:31,783
Tell David to get close to him
for 'healing'.

637
01:29:32,570 --> 01:29:36,570
And get ready to drink his blood.

638
01:29:40,654 --> 01:29:46,054
-Salam Alaikum
-Alaikum Salam.

639
01:29:46,054 --> 01:29:50,924
Welcome, Dündar Bey.
Come, sit.

640
01:29:51,046 --> 01:29:54,206
Thank you.
Thank you.

641
01:29:54,206 --> 01:29:58,946
-Süleyman, let's order food for our bey.
-Right away.

642
01:29:58,946 --> 01:30:03,806
What food, Melik Bey?
We are here to talk trade.

643
01:30:07,614 --> 01:30:09,704
All right.

644
01:30:12,080 --> 01:30:17,020
Are the goods gathered? Are the
caravans on the way? Tell me.

645
01:30:17,031 --> 01:30:24,681
Dündar Bey, when it's about trade,
you don't think of anything else.

646
01:30:25,735 --> 01:30:31,075
If I knew that there was a trader
like you in Söğüt...

647
01:30:31,100 --> 01:30:35,380
...I would bring all my goods to here,
years ago.

648
01:30:35,629 --> 01:30:41,079
Thank you. Thank you.
Better late than never.

649
01:30:41,387 --> 01:30:47,617
From now, Söğüt will be the center
of trade.

650
01:30:47,877 --> 01:30:52,397
-Inshallah.
-We'll trade with distand places.

651
01:30:52,624 --> 01:30:55,574
Thank Allah.
Thank Allah.

652
01:30:58,065 --> 01:31:02,665
-I should treat you with a cold ayran.
-Thank you. Thank you.

653
01:31:14,045 --> 01:31:16,505
What is this?

654
01:31:24,054 --> 01:31:28,054
It's your share, Dündar Bey.

655
01:31:30,423 --> 01:31:34,423
We didn't put enough effort to earn
our share yet.

656
01:31:35,747 --> 01:31:39,747
It's been just a few days.

657
01:31:41,104 --> 01:31:49,994
We declared our intentions, my bey.
Therefore, the business has started for us.

658
01:31:53,929 --> 01:31:59,879
If a trader is giving away coins
before the business starts...

659
01:32:00,314 --> 01:32:04,534
...either they have
things to say...

660
01:32:05,904 --> 01:32:10,314
...or they have a greater plan.

661
01:32:15,123 --> 01:32:19,123
What's your intentions?

662
01:32:28,977 --> 01:32:36,327
Or, in this lion's den,
the trader wants...

663
01:32:38,698 --> 01:32:46,258
...to have an ally to trust
fully, Dündar Bey.

664
01:32:51,279 --> 01:32:55,279
Of course, we made our deal
with Osman Bey.

665
01:32:55,539 --> 01:32:59,539
But if something happens to Osman Bey.

666
01:32:59,890 --> 01:33:03,390
Anything can happen to us here.

667
01:33:05,505 --> 01:33:13,385
For this reason, my master Melik
wants to give this to you as a token.

668
01:33:17,910 --> 01:33:19,950
Thank you.

669
01:33:21,707 --> 01:33:26,557
You are a great helper, Süleyman.

670
01:33:26,773 --> 01:33:32,183
If I had a helper like you,
I would rule all these lands.

671
01:33:32,386 --> 01:33:37,396
-Inshallah, my bey. Inshallah.
-Inshallah.

672
01:33:37,396 --> 01:33:39,386
Inshallah.

673
01:33:43,708 --> 01:33:47,318
Come on now.
I should go.

674
01:33:47,738 --> 01:33:51,738
Inform me when the caravans move.

675
01:33:51,738 --> 01:33:55,738
Then we can talk about how we'll
carry the goods to far away.

676
01:33:56,238 --> 01:34:00,388
All right, may Allah protect you,
my bey.

677
01:34:09,604 --> 01:34:14,794
He is like a wolf in sheep's disguise.

678
01:34:18,286 --> 01:34:23,846
If we dig a little bit more, we'll
take the wolf out of Dündar.

679
01:34:24,196 --> 01:34:28,936
-Huh, 'brother'?
-Yes, 'brother'.

680
01:35:00,654 --> 01:35:05,604
Don't get disturbed as you don't
know these things. He is tracing.

681
01:35:05,887 --> 01:35:09,117
He'll spend the night in somewhere.

682
01:35:10,092 --> 01:35:13,192
Where he is?

683
01:35:13,889 --> 01:35:17,039
How he is?
Who knows.

684
01:35:18,726 --> 01:35:22,726
Of course, he'll come.
Of course.

685
01:35:23,203 --> 01:35:28,333
He doesn't want to leave his hunt
and return. That's how it is.

686
01:35:33,505 --> 01:35:36,345
That's how it is.

687
01:35:43,719 --> 01:35:45,999
Baysungur!

688
01:35:55,249 --> 01:35:59,689
Find two alps who know how to trace.
They should search the hunting sites.

689
01:35:59,689 --> 01:36:03,179
And bring Bayhoca if they find him.

690
01:36:03,467 --> 01:36:05,787
As you order, my bey.

691
01:36:11,390 --> 01:36:15,390
Eat now. Come on.

692
01:36:50,226 --> 01:36:53,358
This is your room, go on.

693
01:37:05,456 --> 01:37:10,876
Lord Nikola appointed this room for you.
If you have a command, tell us.

694
01:37:10,876 --> 01:37:15,266
Good. I'd appreciate it if you bring me
wine at night, pretty girl.

695
01:37:16,437 --> 01:37:20,597
I'll be in your service, sir.
Go on.

696
01:37:44,064 --> 01:37:46,214
They are in their rooms.

697
01:37:54,817 --> 01:37:57,287
I thought your mission to be a game.

698
01:37:58,459 --> 01:38:03,059
Blame it on my youth.
I put Osman Bey's mission...

699
01:38:03,418 --> 01:38:07,288
...and your lives in danger.

700
01:38:07,423 --> 01:38:12,513
-Forgive me.
-My Allah! He is still speaking.

701
01:38:24,184 --> 01:38:29,254
Bayhoca, you are young and brave...

702
01:38:30,553 --> 01:38:35,603
...I see Osman Bey's fire in your eyes.

703
01:38:36,244 --> 01:38:41,074
But to be like Osman Bey...

704
01:38:41,640 --> 01:38:45,800
...you don't know how much
way you still have to go.

705
01:38:48,939 --> 01:38:53,309
Baran Alp, I learn much from
you tonight.

706
01:39:03,852 --> 01:39:06,942
Come on now.

707
01:39:22,210 --> 01:39:26,210
-Welcome, Zülfikar.
-Thank you.

708
01:39:26,890 --> 01:39:31,800
-He is a gift from our Sheikh.
-Thank you.

709
01:39:32,806 --> 01:39:37,306
-Who is this?
-Savcı Bey's son, Bayhoca.

710
01:39:37,976 --> 01:39:42,556
He was passing by.
He wanted to ask how we fare.

711
01:39:44,700 --> 01:39:48,700
Are the lords in their rooms?

712
01:39:55,877 --> 01:40:00,527
This is where the lords' rooms are
There are four guards.

713
01:40:00,530 --> 01:40:05,670
-You should control yourselves.
-Thank you, brother.

714
01:40:06,280 --> 01:40:12,190
I will take you there safe and sound.
May Allah help you.

715
01:40:12,690 --> 01:40:14,700
Come on.

716
01:40:17,386 --> 01:40:25,726
Bayhoca, don't move anywhere. We'll
come and get you. We'll leave together.

717
01:40:25,726 --> 01:40:29,726
As you want, Boran Alp.
May Allah help you.

718
01:40:31,088 --> 01:40:33,598
Come on, brothers.

719
01:41:56,462 --> 01:41:58,972
Gonca.

720
01:42:01,985 --> 01:42:05,825
What are you thinking about?

721
01:42:06,931 --> 01:42:11,781
I'm thinking about my mother, Bala.
My dear mother.

722
01:42:14,022 --> 01:42:18,872
She made these with great care.

723
01:42:19,476 --> 01:42:25,596
I wish, both she and my father...

724
01:42:27,691 --> 01:42:30,981
My beautiful sister.

725
01:42:36,265 --> 01:42:42,665
Who knows? Maybe Sheikh Edebali
will come to your wedding?

726
01:42:43,770 --> 01:42:47,770
-Isn't he our father?
-He is.

727
01:42:49,174 --> 01:42:55,024
After our alps return with victory,
we'll begin the wedding preperations.

728
01:42:55,052 --> 01:42:59,882
Inshallah, Bala.
Inshallah.

729
01:43:05,409 --> 01:43:08,969
The soup kitchen is good, right?

730
01:43:09,986 --> 01:43:14,686
-It made the poor smile.
-It's really good, Bala.

731
01:43:17,971 --> 01:43:21,971
I liked this Aksu Hatun.

732
01:43:23,248 --> 01:43:27,248
She is a pretty woman.

733
01:43:28,933 --> 01:43:32,933
She seems to have a good heart.

734
01:43:35,847 --> 01:43:42,177
I say that we should put her into
a trial.

735
01:43:45,451 --> 01:43:49,451
-If she succeeds--
-So, Bala?

736
01:43:51,608 --> 01:43:55,088
What will happen then?

737
01:43:55,374 --> 01:43:58,724
Then, I will talk to Osman.

738
01:44:01,652 --> 01:44:05,282
I'll mention her.

739
01:44:09,871 --> 01:44:13,211
Maybe he too will like her.

740
01:44:50,508 --> 01:44:53,748
What are you doing here?

741
01:44:53,999 --> 01:44:57,669
We came to tell lullabies to
the lords.

742
01:44:59,797 --> 01:45:03,057
What will you tell us?

743
01:45:03,781 --> 01:45:07,781
Death's sweet lullaby.

744
01:45:35,306 --> 01:45:41,652
Take them away, brother.
Watch out for us. Come.

745
01:47:30,541 --> 01:47:34,541
A trap, huh?
You weasels!

746
01:47:34,600 --> 01:47:37,760
What did you put on
the dagger?

747
01:47:37,760 --> 01:47:41,760
A few medicines.

748
01:47:42,732 --> 01:47:46,322
You will see now.

749
01:49:06,805 --> 01:49:08,668
Nikola!

750
01:49:10,333 --> 01:49:16,943
Did you think this place to be a chicken
coop? Enter as you want...

751
01:49:16,943 --> 01:49:20,943
...take what you want, is that so?
-You will die, dishonorable!

752
01:49:22,614 --> 01:49:26,614
Attack! But don't kill.

753
01:50:01,076 --> 01:50:05,076
What happened? Osman's fox!

754
01:50:05,869 --> 01:50:10,389
Did the sheepdogs of the coon
hurt you? -You will die!

755
01:50:10,941 --> 01:50:13,721
You first.

756
01:50:30,296 --> 01:50:34,776
Take them to the dungeon.
We have a feast tomorrow.

757
01:50:48,562 --> 01:50:51,552
Take him away.

758
01:50:56,677 --> 01:51:01,967
-My brothers won't return before killing
them. -We came anyway, just in case.

759
01:51:01,967 --> 01:51:06,467
They'll give up on their lives but not
return before killing them.

760
01:51:07,489 --> 01:51:11,489
They have 4 lords.

761
01:51:11,736 --> 01:51:18,106
They'll have more important missions
from now on. And about us...

762
01:51:21,036 --> 01:51:25,036
...we have Nikola on our part.

763
01:51:25,036 --> 01:51:30,086
Nikola will die tonight.

764
01:51:30,086 --> 01:51:34,086
-All right, my bey.
-All right.

765
01:51:34,656 --> 01:51:36,396
My bey.

766
01:51:39,953 --> 01:51:42,543
Open it.

767
01:51:56,456 --> 01:52:00,776
Eftelya, what happened?

768
01:52:00,776 --> 01:52:04,216
They got caught, Osman Bey.

769
01:52:05,175 --> 01:52:10,755
-They were taken to the dungeon.
-My bey, let's fire this dark night.

770
01:52:10,840 --> 01:52:15,480
I pity us if we leave before taking our
brothers and killing these dogs.

771
01:52:17,311 --> 01:52:22,161
Take us to the dungeon.
Do you know a way?

772
01:52:23,422 --> 01:52:25,222
Thank you.

773
01:52:25,962 --> 01:52:30,812
Eftelya, keep your eyes on Nikola.

774
01:53:14,519 --> 01:53:17,319
Dishonorable dogs!

775
01:53:31,545 --> 01:53:33,865
Enough!

776
01:54:29,550 --> 01:54:33,170
From now, it's on us.

777
01:54:33,170 --> 01:54:36,170
You are left to me from my father.

778
01:54:36,905 --> 01:54:40,395
Protect yourself and
your daughter.

779
01:54:40,688 --> 01:54:47,338
In return for your service, people will
live with justice and freedom.

780
01:54:47,817 --> 01:54:51,117
I'll show it to the whole world.

781
01:54:51,587 --> 01:54:57,557
This is the parole of Osman Bey
son of Ertuğrul Ghazi.

782
01:55:00,816 --> 01:55:03,326
Give me your blessing.

783
01:55:07,566 --> 01:55:09,736
Come on.

784
01:55:37,675 --> 01:55:41,675
My bey, how could they get
caught?

785
01:55:42,609 --> 01:55:46,609
I trust them completely.

786
01:55:46,932 --> 01:55:50,072
We'll find out later.

787
01:55:53,137 --> 01:55:57,717
-Give me your blessings.
-It's yours, my bey.

788
01:55:58,021 --> 01:56:00,071
It's yours, my bey.

789
01:56:01,947 --> 01:56:05,027
May Allah help us.

790
01:56:21,831 --> 01:56:24,491
Let him go!

791
01:56:25,263 --> 01:56:26,893
Let him go!

792
01:56:30,256 --> 01:56:34,236
You ignoble dogs!

793
01:56:34,477 --> 01:56:36,707
Let them go!

794
01:56:45,641 --> 01:56:48,151
Did you hurt your hand, dog?

795
01:56:48,192 --> 01:56:51,782
Let's see how strong you are!

796
01:56:52,205 --> 01:56:57,025
My Bey, those are our guys.

797
01:56:57,257 --> 01:56:59,327
They are alive, my Bey.

798
01:57:09,992 --> 01:57:11,812
Let's go.

799
01:57:23,606 --> 01:57:27,046
Osman Bey!
Kill Osman!

800
01:57:53,502 --> 01:57:56,852
I am here Boran brother, hold on!

801
01:58:05,936 --> 01:58:08,476
My Bey!

802
01:58:09,649 --> 01:58:11,449
Brothers!

803
01:58:18,402 --> 01:58:21,462
My Bey, what are you doing here?

804
01:58:21,462 --> 01:58:24,072
I don't leave my brothers alone.

805
01:58:34,581 --> 01:58:40,381
My Bey, forgive us.
We failed the duty.

806
01:58:41,161 --> 01:58:46,421
Boran, tell me, how did you get caught?

807
01:58:47,115 --> 01:58:50,405
Do we have a spy in us?

808
01:58:54,299 --> 01:58:59,969
You got beat up to a pulp, Gence Bey.

809
01:59:00,283 --> 01:59:02,563
They medicated us.

810
01:59:04,658 --> 01:59:08,548
What happened Boran?
How did you get caught?

811
01:59:08,550 --> 01:59:14,630
- Apparently, they waited for you here.
- I don't know my Bey, but Bayhoca...

812
01:59:16,768 --> 01:59:18,902
What happened to Bayhoca?

813
01:59:18,902 --> 01:59:22,512
Bayhoca was here when we arrived, my Bey.

814
01:59:25,266 --> 01:59:27,196
What are you talking about?

815
01:59:32,065 --> 01:59:35,535
He followed us secretly.

816
01:59:40,717 --> 01:59:43,497
Just like your younger days, my Bey.

817
01:59:49,322 --> 01:59:52,772
Let's get out of here before soldiers
find us, my Bey.

818
02:00:08,248 --> 02:00:09,938
Let's go.

819
02:01:17,912 --> 02:01:20,352
I think I know you.

820
02:01:23,452 --> 02:01:24,722
Right?

821
02:01:28,250 --> 02:01:33,410
These eyes, this look.

822
02:01:34,893 --> 02:01:36,743
This jaw...

823
02:01:38,832 --> 02:01:46,082
You must be very close to him as he
assigned you to this mission.

824
02:01:51,661 --> 02:01:54,771
But I have not seen you with him before.

825
02:01:56,037 --> 02:01:59,997
Tell me your name young man.

826
02:02:05,496 --> 02:02:08,866
So you are going to keep your silence.

827
02:02:19,135 --> 02:02:22,705
Now tell us who you are.

828
02:02:22,892 --> 02:02:26,682
- Go to hell Nicola!
- Stop!

829
02:02:35,062 --> 02:02:39,949
You are going to accompany me to there,
young man.

830
02:02:40,039 --> 02:02:46,539
By the way we caught the alps who came to
raid us.

831
02:02:48,314 --> 02:02:53,984
Do you know why?
Because of your clumsiness.

832
02:02:54,106 --> 02:02:58,137
Search all the rooms!
Close the exits!

833
02:02:58,137 --> 02:03:01,647
Search this one!
Why have not they arrived yet?

834
02:03:03,033 --> 02:03:06,313
There's someone here ma'am.

835
02:03:09,616 --> 02:03:13,866
Who are you?
What are you doing here?

836
02:03:13,940 --> 02:03:17,770
I am a musician.

837
02:03:17,805 --> 02:03:22,102
I drank wine a bit much.

838
02:03:22,102 --> 02:03:25,212
You are coming from Bilecik, right?

839
02:03:28,249 --> 02:03:33,659
I can sing you a lovely song.

840
02:04:16,048 --> 02:04:17,818
Liar!

841
02:04:18,163 --> 02:04:20,373
You are lying!

842
02:04:29,974 --> 02:04:32,664
I wish I was dead.

843
02:04:33,672 --> 02:04:38,069
I can't stand the sadness of a young man
like you.

844
02:04:38,069 --> 02:04:43,589
Don't you worry. I am going to hang you
all with a great ceremony.

845
02:04:51,253 --> 02:04:54,883
My uncle Osman Bey...

846
02:04:57,490 --> 02:05:01,070
will make you pay for the blood you shed!

847
02:05:06,551 --> 02:05:10,501
He'll ruin you all.

848
02:05:12,925 --> 02:05:16,255
My uncle Osman...

849
02:05:33,221 --> 02:05:36,741
Are you Savcı's son?

850
02:05:40,486 --> 02:05:43,026
Lena's son...

851
02:05:44,692 --> 02:05:48,032
Bayhoca, right?

852
02:05:51,173 --> 02:05:54,713
Have you heard what I've heard, Vladius?

853
02:05:54,732 --> 02:05:59,812
Nicola, we hit the bullseye, Nicola.

854
02:06:01,961 --> 02:06:07,811
So these eyes, these looks...

855
02:06:08,993 --> 02:06:12,933
You are that old chap's grandson.

856
02:06:15,966 --> 02:06:20,876
Kill me.
Kill me!

857
02:06:21,016 --> 02:06:24,416
Kill me, think that you won!

858
02:06:25,366 --> 02:06:28,186
I am not in hurry, young man.

859
02:06:29,358 --> 02:06:33,531
I am sure your uncle Osman will come
for you.

860
02:06:33,531 --> 02:06:37,481
Even for a last time, right Vladius?

861
02:06:47,185 --> 02:06:50,445
Bayhoca...

862
02:06:53,853 --> 02:06:57,573
Let's see what your uncle Osman is
going to do!

863
02:07:58,485 --> 02:08:01,915
My Bey, Bayhoca must be waiting for us.

864
02:08:03,933 --> 02:08:05,763
He is not, Boran.

865
02:08:06,352 --> 02:08:09,512
My Bey, what are you talking about?

866
02:08:11,067 --> 02:08:14,157
- They caught him.
- No, my Bey.

867
02:08:14,325 --> 02:08:17,055
Nobody realized him.

868
02:08:18,367 --> 02:08:24,947
They caught him, then they realized
we are going to the governor.

869
02:08:27,978 --> 02:08:31,538
They planned medicines and everything.

870
02:08:31,641 --> 02:08:37,431
That's why Eftelye, Aruton and Zulfikar
knew everything.

871
02:08:39,475 --> 02:08:41,555
Are we going to leave him here my Bey?

872
02:08:43,928 --> 02:08:50,988
They won't kill my nephew.
Their aim is to get me.

873
02:08:52,604 --> 02:08:57,628
Now we are getting out of the castle.
Then, we will come back and raid them.

874
02:08:57,628 --> 02:09:00,478
- Eyvallah my Bey.
- Eyvallah.

875
02:09:49,367 --> 02:09:52,157
It's been late, he is still absent.

876
02:09:55,298 --> 02:09:58,588
Something bad must have happened.

877
02:10:02,446 --> 02:10:05,866
They realised my son is a Kayı Bey.

878
02:10:10,600 --> 02:10:13,830
They captured my son.

879
02:10:18,147 --> 02:10:20,547
Maybe..

880
02:10:22,582 --> 02:10:25,522
- Maybe...
- Lena Hatun.

881
02:10:27,051 --> 02:10:28,831
Don't wory.

882
02:10:31,166 --> 02:10:33,696
We'll find him eventually.

883
02:10:34,203 --> 02:10:36,133
We'll hear from him eventually.

884
02:10:37,610 --> 02:10:40,760
Our son will come back safe and sound.

885
02:10:41,589 --> 02:10:46,869
Also, no one can dare to hurt him.

886
02:10:49,401 --> 02:10:52,411
Who can hurt Savcı's son?

887
02:10:54,014 --> 02:11:01,404
I'ld make them regret,
don't you know, Hatun?

888
02:11:08,752 --> 02:11:11,422
What are you talking about Savcı Bey?

889
02:11:12,803 --> 02:11:17,053
What am I going to do with revenge
if something bad happens to my son?

890
02:11:18,751 --> 02:11:23,641
If they hurt him..

891
02:11:25,271 --> 02:11:29,791
Lena... Oh Lena.

892
02:11:44,365 --> 02:11:46,965
Find him Savcı.

893
02:12:03,118 --> 02:12:06,488
Sir, Osman took the captives.

894
02:12:08,381 --> 02:12:11,861
My valiant uncle, god bless him!

895
02:12:15,765 --> 02:12:18,780
He was in the castle all the time!

896
02:12:18,780 --> 02:12:22,910
I know where to find Osman, Nicola!
He'll come for his nephew!

897
02:12:23,104 --> 02:12:25,224
Open the door!

898
02:12:27,027 --> 02:12:30,727
First Kulucahisar, then my castle!

899
02:12:30,821 --> 02:12:36,181
Do not I have soldiers to stop this man?

900
02:12:36,319 --> 02:12:39,729
Can't we lock this man down!?

901
02:13:40,579 --> 02:13:44,838
You are fine, thank God, Osman Bey.
They captured Bayhoca.

902
02:13:44,838 --> 02:13:47,278
I saw them taking him to Governor's room.

903
02:13:47,278 --> 02:13:49,988
I know. I know.

904
02:13:50,571 --> 02:13:54,741
Take us back from where we came.
Wait for our sign.

905
02:13:54,919 --> 02:13:57,789
I am going to be back for Bayhoca.

906
02:14:20,584 --> 02:14:22,984
Find 'em!

907
02:14:29,616 --> 02:14:33,386
- He went after Osman's alps.
- Enough, Hatun!

908
02:14:33,423 --> 02:14:36,031
We are going to find him!

909
02:14:36,031 --> 02:14:38,611
- Can I, my Bey?
- Come in, Baysungur.

910
02:14:40,941 --> 02:14:43,291
Tell me what's new.

911
02:14:43,807 --> 02:14:47,177
Osman Bey is waiting for you, my Bey.

912
02:14:55,262 --> 02:15:00,102
Is there anyting about my son, Bayhoca?

913
02:15:05,811 --> 02:15:07,221
Tell me.

914
02:15:10,006 --> 02:15:11,996
Speak!

915
02:15:15,264 --> 02:15:21,704
Speak up, Savcı Bey. Ask about Bayhoca.
Ask him what this is about!

916
02:15:27,959 --> 02:15:32,861
Speak!
Tell me if it's about my son.

917
02:15:32,861 --> 02:15:35,251
Is he hurt?

918
02:15:35,326 --> 02:15:39,346
Enoguh Lena!
Enough.

919
02:15:40,375 --> 02:15:44,285
It must be important.
Let's go to the tent.

920
02:16:17,556 --> 02:16:22,066
My son, Bayhoca.

921
02:16:31,406 --> 02:16:32,996
Osman Bey.

922
02:16:35,608 --> 02:16:38,678
Is there anything about my Son?

923
02:16:44,272 --> 02:16:47,192
Is my son fine?

924
02:16:49,253 --> 02:16:52,283
Tell me Osman Bey, is my son fine?

925
02:17:00,816 --> 02:17:03,856
Where is my son, Osman Bey?

926
02:17:08,990 --> 02:17:15,410
Bayhoca went after my Alps to
Inegol Castle.

927
02:17:23,819 --> 02:17:27,289
Didn't they realise that my son
followed them?

928
02:17:28,809 --> 02:17:33,379
Osman Bey, what's my son's situation?

929
02:17:39,249 --> 02:17:41,739
My Alps got caught.

930
02:17:42,967 --> 02:17:47,087
- I saved them but...
- But?

931
02:17:48,957 --> 02:17:51,677
My son Bayhoca?

932
02:17:52,537 --> 02:17:55,597
Did you leave him there, Osman Bey?

933
02:18:00,566 --> 02:18:04,286
You saved your Alps and sacrificed my son?

934
02:18:04,333 --> 02:18:07,863
- Did you sacrifice my son, Osman Bey?
- Lena!

935
02:18:08,675 --> 02:18:10,795
Enough already.

936
02:18:17,380 --> 02:18:23,910
My Brother, where is my son?
What's his situation?

937
02:18:25,449 --> 02:18:27,469
Tell me.

938
02:18:34,696 --> 02:18:37,256
He got captured by Nicola.

939
02:18:40,938 --> 02:18:44,738
No. No.

940
02:18:47,560 --> 02:18:50,100
No he can't be.

941
02:18:51,859 --> 02:18:53,639
No.

942
02:19:00,772 --> 02:19:02,672
No way.

943
02:19:07,150 --> 02:19:12,130
How can you leave my son Osman Bey?
How can you!

944
02:19:12,348 --> 02:19:16,270
- Lena!
- How can you sacrifice my son, Osman Bey?

945
02:19:16,270 --> 02:19:19,130
- Lena!
- Tell me!

946
02:19:19,472 --> 02:19:20,612
Brother.

947
02:19:21,443 --> 02:19:25,513
How can you sacrifice my young valiant,
Osman Bey?

948
02:19:26,695 --> 02:19:29,205
My young valiant.

949
02:19:31,649 --> 02:19:36,559
How can you leave him there with
the murderers, Osman Bey?

950
02:19:37,058 --> 02:19:39,158
Tell me!

951
02:19:42,679 --> 02:19:46,009
Tell me!
How could you?

952
02:19:52,506 --> 02:19:55,766
Bayhoca is still alive.

953
02:20:00,207 --> 02:20:03,757
How can you know that, ha?

954
02:20:04,887 --> 02:20:09,572
- How can you know that?
- They won't kill my nephew.

955
02:20:11,108 --> 02:20:13,938
They'll use him against me.

956
02:20:20,102 --> 02:20:23,092
What if they kill him?

957
02:20:26,200 --> 02:20:29,794
What if they kill my son, Osman Bey?

958
02:20:29,794 --> 02:20:31,924
Lena!

959
02:20:32,506 --> 02:20:34,296
He wanted to be Ghazi.

960
02:20:37,524 --> 02:20:41,034
Ghazis end up with shahada.

961
02:20:52,321 --> 02:20:56,391
You killed my son by leaving
him in the castle for once, Osman Bey.

962
02:20:58,187 --> 02:21:01,053
But you killed my one thousand times.

963
02:21:01,053 --> 02:21:03,763
You killed me one thousand times!

964
02:21:06,222 --> 02:21:10,886
Shame on you!
Shame on you!

965
02:21:10,886 --> 02:21:12,426
Lena!

966
02:21:18,234 --> 02:21:20,834
I wish you were the captive!

967
02:21:22,987 --> 02:21:27,027
I wish you were the captive, not my son
Osman Bey1

968
02:21:38,120 --> 02:21:40,980
My Bey, a messenger from the
castle came.

969
02:22:00,265 --> 02:22:03,255
If you don't give Kulucahisar back...

970
02:22:07,476 --> 02:22:10,586
I'll kill Bayhoca.

971
02:23:03,458 --> 02:23:06,738
No!
Savcı!

972
02:23:32,181 --> 02:23:33,871
Bayhoca...

973
02:23:34,209 --> 02:23:36,069
Bayhoca!

974
02:23:40,320 --> 02:23:43,450
If I return without my nephew...

975
02:23:45,232 --> 02:23:47,402
My horse shall be my coffin.

976
02:23:49,831 --> 02:23:53,461
My tent shall be my coffin!

977
02:23:54,518 --> 02:23:59,798
If I don't keep my word..

978
02:24:01,358 --> 02:24:07,658
Ertuğrul Ghazi's tent shall be my tomb!

979
02:24:07,841 --> 02:24:16,191
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com